  {
    "episode_id": 87541,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/7/87541.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "This is the Fox News rundown. Extra. I'm Dave Anthony. Today, a look into a future where more of what's real will be artificial. This past week, a House bipartisan AI task force issued its final report as this Congress comes to a close, going in depth about how far-reaching artificial intelligence will become and what the government should do to regulate it and foster it and how AI affects everything from our identities to the business world and the personal and national security protections we need as the technology keeps expanding. And we talked to a co-chair on that task force, Congressman J. Obernolte, a Republican from California, who as you'll hear has for years been fascinated and studied AI. The conversation we had about it was too long to fit in through the rundown podcast the other day, including his past work in the video game business. We think you'll find interesting. We had to cut that. But today, it's all there in our weekend extra. We post these every Saturday and Sunday in addition to our daily new rundown content. So we urge you to keep coming back. Thank you as always for listening. Happy holidays. And now Congressman J. Obernolte on the Fox News rundown extra. joining us on the fox news rundown is congressman j over knulty he is a republican representing california in the twenty-third district is there a congressman twenty-third right twenty third of california yep california twenty third art uh... just reelected by the way uh... for another term and you were the co-chair of the bipartisan house task force on a i studying it going through it for all these months and have a final report out this week first of all we appreciate being here congressman thanks for joining us",
