        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Government intervention through legislation is necessary to mitigate risks without stifling innovation.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The U.S. government, specifically Congress, possesses both the competence and legitimacy to regulate complex technological systems.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Technological progress should be balanced with public safety and national security concerns.",
        "confidence": 0.88
